      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO DETERMINERS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Determiners are words placed before nouns to clarify quantity, possession, distance, or distribution.",
        "Differentiate correctly between Few/A Few/The Few (countable) and Little/A Little/The Little (uncountable).",
        "Each refers to individual members of a definite group, whereas Every refers to all members collectively.",
        "Avoiding double determiner usage is essential for passing SSC sentence correction questions."
      ],
      "id": "ddz70id"
    },
